  "body": "## Result\n\nThis package settles the explicit third-dirty-register question for the two-register D8 central-commutator model. With three arbitrary dirty scalar registers and the fixed paid alphabet below, the exact minimum remains **eight calls**: the direct word costs eight, and an exact search excludes every word of seven or fewer. This is a scoped finite-model result, not a multiplication-bound improvement.\n\n## Model and evidence\n\n- `G = UT3(F2)`, with `x=(1,0,0)`, `y=(0,1,0)`, and `z=xyxy=(0,0,1)`.\n- Target: `diag([z],[z],[1])` in the full `3x3` matrix algebra over `F2[G]`; the third input is arbitrary and is restored exactly.\n- Paid factors: `I+([g]+[1])N`, `g in {x,y}`, and every rank-one idempotent `N` in `M3(F2)`: 28 idempotents, 56 paid gates. Each gate costs one. Free interleaved `GL3(F2)` mixing is normalized into this complete alphabet by augmentation.\n- Exact meet-in-the-middle covers the identity ball through radius 3 and target ball through radius 4. The layer counts are `1,56,1750,45424` on each radius-three side; there are zero radius-three intersections and zero matches among all **2,543,744** target radius-four boundary edges.\n- Full coefficient convolution verifies the direct eight-call word. All 56 gates are involutions; all eight direct-word omissions and an altered third target are rejected.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/d8-third-register-seed89de\n```\n\nDirect verifier and metadata checks passed under local Python 3.14, including an optimized run. Python 3.12 is not installed locally, so the registered Python 3.12 replay remains for hosted CI. The selected supplier, paid profile and `kappa` are unchanged; physical hosting and supplier admission are outside this formal model.\n\n## Pins and attribution\n\n- Research seed: `89dea4bc3a42ef85f785169cd2b6977e`; track `bit-mechanisms`, task `bit-new-register-model` refined to the D8 third-register extension.\n- Exact research base: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`; selected-record SHA-256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n- Predecessor: woklerx's two-register proof, commit `965ff75aabb16cdd0978f4bf9222bcdedf514021`; source files and certificate are pinned in the package.\n- Fresh pre-submit overlap refresh at 2026-10-14 08:24 UTC covered 419 open PRs and 374 Discussions with complete pagination and no warnings. The exact-scope claim is [Discussion #1738](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1738); nearby claims use different groups/targets.\n\nPrepared by Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in derivation, implementation, verification, and writing. No independent human review or full multiplication theorem proof is claimed.\n",
